# `scripts/` is not excluded any more, and the reason is worth writing down.
#
# The image's builder stage runs the type check over the whole tree, and the
# tree is what the build context carries. With `scripts/` excluded, the
# checker in the image could not see the scripts the unit tests import, and
# reported them as missing modules -- errors that existed only inside the
# image, on a tree that checks clean everywhere else.
#
# The scripts never reach the shipped image: the runner stage copies
# `.next/standalone`, `.next/static`, `public` and `messages`, and nothing
# else. Excluding them from the context kept a megabyte out of a builder
# layer, and cost the image the ability to check the tree it was built from.
